Work done to accelerate from 0 to $v$ is, $W_{1}=\frac{1}{2} m v^{2}$ Work done to accelerate from $v$ to $2 v$ is,
$\begin{aligned}
W_{2} &=\frac{1}{2} m(2 v)^{2} \\
\Delta W &=W_{2}-W_{1}=\frac{1}{2} m(2 v)^{2}-\frac{1}{2} m v^{2} \\
\Rightarrow \quad & 4 W_{1}-W_{1}=3 W_{1}
\end{aligned}$

By work energy theorem,
and $\quad \mathrm{Fs}_{2}=\frac{1}{2} \mathrm{ m}(2 \mathrm{x})^{2}$
From Eqs. (i) and (ii), s_{2}=4 s_{1}
